1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,350
Working nights at a petrol station,

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,665
you learn to spot the weird ones.

3
00:00:04,715 --> 00:00:07,405
This one stood outside the automatic doors.

4
00:00:07,455 --> 00:00:09,181
They wouldn't open for him.

5
00:00:09,231 --> 00:00:12,603
So he knocked on the glass and asked if he could come in.

6
00:00:12,673 --> 00:00:13,513
You said yes.

7
00:00:13,563 --> 00:00:14,378
Obviously.

8
00:00:14,428 --> 00:00:15,565
It's a shop.

9
00:00:15,715 --> 00:00:17,255
He bought a bag of rice.

10
00:00:17,305 --> 00:00:20,009
Paid in coins from seventeen ninety.

11
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,985
And on the CCTV screen,

12
00:00:22,035 --> 00:00:23,751
you were serving nobody.

13
00:00:24,141 --> 00:00:26,266
He leaned over the counter and said,

14
00:00:26,316 --> 00:00:27,599
you look tired.

15
00:00:27,649 --> 00:00:28,771
Then nothing.

16
00:00:29,321 --> 00:00:31,596
You wake up on the floor at three thirty-three.

17
00:00:31,646 --> 00:00:32,846
The till's full.

18
00:00:32,896 --> 00:00:34,339
Nothing's missing.

19
00:00:34,389 --> 00:00:36,319
Except the rice is everywhere.

20
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:37,896
And you're counting it.

21
00:00:38,046 --> 00:00:39,696
You decide you dozed off.

22
00:00:39,746 --> 00:00:41,381
You finish the shift.

23
00:00:41,531 --> 00:00:42,171
By five,

24
00:00:42,221 --> 00:00:44,590
coffee smells like burning hair.

25
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:47,941
And you can hear the heartbeat of the man at pump four.

26
00:00:48,251 --> 00:00:49,211
At ten to six,

27
00:00:49,261 --> 00:00:50,716
the sky goes grey.

28
00:00:50,766 --> 00:00:53,365
The back of your hand starts to smoke.

29
00:00:53,515 --> 00:00:55,020
Your shift ends at six.

30
00:00:55,070 --> 00:00:57,259
Sunrise is six twelve.

31
00:00:57,329 --> 00:00:58,559
And on his receipt,

32
00:00:58,609 --> 00:01:00,469
he's left a phone number.
